WEBVTT

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.520
[glass cracks]

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:28.000
[birds chirping]

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.000
[panting]

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:05.760
[phone beeps]

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.840
[beeps]

00:01:10.840 --> 00:01:13.560
-[man] Hey, Lacie!
-Hey! [giggles]

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:14.720
[phone beeps]

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:26.520
[camera clicks]

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.320
["send" alert plays]

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:30.920
[phone beeps]

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.440
[giggles]

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.680
[giggles]

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.240
[giggles]

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.920
[laughing hysterically]

00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.080
[Lacie] Ryan?

00:02:11.160 --> 00:02:12.720
[combat sounds on headset]

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:14.080
Ryan!

00:02:19.160 --> 00:02:21.280
-[yells]
-[explosion on headset]

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:24.040
-I was holding a bomb!
-[man] <i>Come on!</i>

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.640
Sorry, guys.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:31.400
Landlord is sending buyers over today
so... put your pants on.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:35.760
Maybe if I don't,
it'll scare 'em off and we can stay here.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.200
[singsong] Not an option, Ryan.
Lease is up in four weeks.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:41.320
Hey, I'm thinking of you.
I've got somewhere to go.

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:45.800
Nate's roommate took a job in Phoenix
so I get his place.

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:49.080
-Okay.
-Now who's the slow poke?

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:54.600
I'm... seeing some places over lunch.
Catch you later.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.760
[gunfire on headset]

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:01.840
Sorry, that was my sister.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.600
Yeah. Yeah, I bet you'd love to.

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.240
[man] Jasmine tea?

00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.000
[child giggles]

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:21.640
[phone beeps]

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.720
[man] And that's one Brushed Suede.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.360
You want a cookie with that?

00:03:29.440 --> 00:03:33.040
-It's on the house.
-Sounds awesome. [giggles]

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:38.320
-[Lacie giggles]
-[phone beeps]

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:41.160
-See you tomorrow, JJ.
-See you, Lacie.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:42.240
[laughs]

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:46.440
[gasps] Oh, I saw your boy
in the fire hat just now! So cute!

00:03:46.520 --> 00:03:49.080
-Yeah, he's really something.
-[laughs]

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.600
[phone beeps]

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.800
[chuckles softly]

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:28.080
[laughs]

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:33.640
[camera shutter clicks]

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:36.880
Hmm.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.320
[phone beeps]

00:04:56.880 --> 00:04:59.600
[phone beeps repeatedly]

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.000
[elevator bell dings]

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:15.520
Hey, Lacie!

00:05:15.600 --> 00:05:18.960
-Bets, it's great to see you!
-You too.

00:05:19.040 --> 00:05:20.040
[Lacie giggles]

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:30.400
[cat meows]

00:05:30.480 --> 00:05:31.800
[Lacie] How's Pancakes?

00:05:31.880 --> 00:05:36.080
He's hilarious.
Such a funny cat. Just the best.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:37.320
[both laugh]

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.280
-Are you still at Hoddicker?
-Mm-hmm.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:45.400
-Yeah. It's going pretty great.
-Good to hear.

00:05:45.480 --> 00:05:47.640
-So what brings you back here?
-New job, first day.

00:05:47.720 --> 00:05:50.160
-First day?
-At Blankman-Harper.

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:53.080
Whoa! Top floor! That's...

00:05:53.160 --> 00:05:56.520
-Well, good luck.
-I know, right? [laughs]

00:05:57.880 --> 00:06:00.920
It's great you're still happy
at Hoddicker.

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.240
-Well, maybe not forever.
-No, not forever.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:04.960
-But for now...
-It's OK for now.

00:06:05.040 --> 00:06:08.600
It's great for now, yes. Yes, it is.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:12.840
[chattering]

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:16.760
[phone ringing]

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:24.480
[phone beeps]

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.760
[beeping]

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.960
[waves crashing, seagulls squawk]

00:07:05.680 --> 00:07:08.560
Lacie, I got you a smoothie.

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:12.400
Got one for everyone, actually.
Still a bunch of them for grabs.

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:16.280
They're from the organic stall
at the farmers' market.

00:07:16.360 --> 00:07:17.840
Sure. Okay.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.000
[gasps]

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:26.160
Mmm!

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.280
[phone beeps]

00:07:32.600 --> 00:07:34.600
Thank you. Thank you.

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.320
[whispers]
We're kind of not talking to Ches.

00:07:42.600 --> 00:07:46.440
-3.1? What happened?
-Him and Gordon split up.

00:07:46.520 --> 00:07:47.960
Oh...

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.920
-Poor Ches.
-No, no, no, we're all on Gordon's side.

00:07:51.000 --> 00:07:53.680
Sure! Obviously.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:57.280
Ches is kissing ass.
Trying to scrape himself back.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:01.760
Of course, if it drops below two-five,
then it's... bye-bye.

00:08:01.840 --> 00:08:03.720
[phone beeps]

00:08:04.760 --> 00:08:06.440
[both gasp]

00:08:08.760 --> 00:08:10.120
[phone beeps]

00:08:12.280 --> 00:08:16.080
[phone beeping]

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:30.200
[ringtone chiming]

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.080
[Lacie] Hello?

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:37.080
-[Ryan]<i> Yo, they're taking it.</i>
-Who?

00:08:37.160 --> 00:08:40.400
<i>The couple the landlord sent over.</i>
<i>I heard them talking.</i>

00:08:40.480 --> 00:08:41.520
Okay.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:48.560
So,
now we move into the light space area.

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:52.520
Ideal for special times with loved ones.

00:08:52.600 --> 00:08:56.560
-Great food, great company.
-Mm-hmm!

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.720
-[phone beeps]
-Whoa! [laughs]

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.280
[woman]
Sampled your photo stream to make her.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:06.840
Great hair!

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:08.960
[woman] Styled free of charge
at the members' salon.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:12.920
Oh, my God. [giggles]

00:09:14.440 --> 00:09:16.160
[Lacie] It's hilarious!

00:09:16.240 --> 00:09:18.880
[woman] You like him?

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.000
-He's okay.
-He doesn't come with the apartment.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.560
[both laugh]

00:09:25.480 --> 00:09:29.320
But there is a bar and restaurant
on site, tenants only.

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:33.520
We have unparalleled metrics
on romantic geneses.

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:34.640
Uh-huh.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:38.160
[woman] I gotta say,
these places are going like "that."

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.360
-So don't delay if you're interested.
-Oh, I'm more than interested.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:46.240
Standard occupancy
on a minimum six-month contract,

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.760
we're talking... this much.

00:09:51.320 --> 00:09:54.040
-How often are the payments?
-That's weekly.

00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.400
-Okay.
-[woman laughs]

00:09:56.480 --> 00:09:58.840
-A little more than expected?
-Yeah.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.120
There's options.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:02.600
You know our Prime Influencers Programme?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:05.400
-Do I qualify for that?
-No. No, you don't.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.600
We'd need you around a 4.5.

00:10:10.280 --> 00:10:12.600
4.5?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.840
Hit 4.5 and there's a 20% discount.

00:10:19.880 --> 00:10:21.760
-4.5.
-That's right.

00:10:26.200 --> 00:10:27.800
[sighs]

00:10:30.040 --> 00:10:31.760
[laughs]

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.000
[sighs]

00:10:38.120 --> 00:10:39.800
[laughter]

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.320
[beeps]

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.040
[laughs softly]

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:21.640
Pelican Cove? What is this?
A eugenics programme?

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:26.640
-A lifestyle community.
-No one is this happy.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:29.160
A two-year-old with a fucking balloon
isn't this happy.

00:11:29.240 --> 00:11:31.880
It's actually a pretty cool place.

00:11:33.600 --> 00:11:36.040
Like you'd even qualify.

00:11:42.600 --> 00:11:44.200
There's nothing I can do, sir.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:46.720
[man] Well, it's not hopeless,
you're clearly a tryer.

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:50.280
That's the sense you get just from... me?

00:11:50.360 --> 00:11:52.960
From your rep report analytics.

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:56.600
If we drill down into the numbers,
you've got a solid popularity arc here.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:00.160
Strong overall trajectory.
Let's just look at the last 24 hours.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.160
You see, even--

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:06.400
What's that? 8:40 a.m.
You're working hard on your socials.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:08.440
-Great little uptake there.
-Okay.

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:11.800
Couple of minor dings there.
You cut someone off in traffic?

00:12:11.880 --> 00:12:14.720
Oh, just a workplace thing. [laughs]

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:17.760
Okay.
Let's check on your sphere of influence.

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:19.880
Let me zoom out here.

00:12:20.840 --> 00:12:24.160
Great peripherals.
Strangers like you, that's a plus.

00:12:24.240 --> 00:12:28.800
-Healthy inner circle. It's good.
-Thank you. [giggles]

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:32.440
There's a ways to go, 
but 4.5 is certainly achievable.

00:12:33.160 --> 00:12:34.480
How long do you think?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.680
-To hit 4.5?
-Mm-hmm.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.760
Well, barring a major setback,

00:12:37.840 --> 00:12:42.000
a public disgrace kind of deal,
I'd say 18 months or so.

00:12:43.160 --> 00:12:47.480
Oh, I need more short term.
Like... much more. [laughs]

00:12:47.560 --> 00:12:48.840
Then you'll need a boost.

00:12:49.720 --> 00:12:51.920
-What kind of a boost?
-Well...

00:12:53.400 --> 00:12:56.160
Most of your interactions are confined
to your inner circle

00:12:56.240 --> 00:13:00.680
and they're largely, pardon the term,
mid- to low-range folks.

00:13:00.760 --> 00:13:02.120
Same with your outer circle.

00:13:02.200 --> 00:13:05.400
You've got a ton of reciprocal five stars
from service industry workers,

00:13:05.480 --> 00:13:07.360
but there's not much else.

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.160
At least as far as I can see.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:12.000
So in terms of quality,
you could use a punch up right there.

00:13:12.080 --> 00:13:15.240
Ideally,
that's up votes from quality people.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.720
-Quality people?
-High fours.

00:13:18.800 --> 00:13:22.360
Impress those up-scale folks,
you'll gain velocity on your arc

00:13:22.440 --> 00:13:24.080
and there's your boost.

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:27.120
[phone beeps]

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:35.800
[panting]

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.640
-Oh, hi, JJ!
-Hey, Lacie!

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:43.800
-Keith! Hello.
-Lacie!

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:47.000
-[Keith] You look great today.
-Thank you!

00:13:47.960 --> 00:13:51.880
-Door won't open. I'm on 2.4.
-Sorry, Ches. I'm late.

00:13:51.960 --> 00:13:53.880
I just need some stars, please!

00:13:55.800 --> 00:13:57.120
Fuck!

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:01.960
[elevator bell dings]

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:08.320
-Oh, hi!
-Hi!

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.680
-How's it going at Blankman?
-Just great.

00:14:11.760 --> 00:14:16.960
-Well, I bet you work... good there.
-Thank you.

00:14:21.520 --> 00:14:23.280
Would you like a croissant?

00:14:23.360 --> 00:14:25.480
They gave me an extra at the coffee place.

00:14:25.560 --> 00:14:28.680
-Oh, no, I already ate.
-Okay, sure. All good. Yes.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:30.000
Yeah.

00:14:32.040 --> 00:14:36.640
-[elevator bell dings]
-Well, here's me, so...

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:40.680
-[giggles]
-[phones beep]

00:14:44.320 --> 00:14:47.160
<i>Don't try too hard.</i>
<i>It's impossible to respect.</i>

00:14:47.240 --> 00:14:51.680
<i>High fours can smell it a mile off.</i>
<i>Just be you.</i>

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:54.000
<i>Authentic gestures, that's the key.</i>

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:57.520
<i>-That's time up, I'll catch you later.</i>
-Oh, could I just ask--

00:15:11.680 --> 00:15:12.760
[phone chirps]

00:15:23.640 --> 00:15:25.280
[beeping]

00:15:51.680 --> 00:15:52.480
[camera clicks]

00:15:54.840 --> 00:15:55.960
[chirps]

00:16:00.680 --> 00:16:05.000
[mutters] ..."Mr. Rags."

00:16:09.760 --> 00:16:11.640
[exhales]

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:22.400
[sighs]

00:16:23.520 --> 00:16:25.080
[beeps]

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:36.760
[laughs]

00:16:42.160 --> 00:16:43.520
[gasps]

00:16:44.000 --> 00:16:44.920
Shit!

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:58.880
-What the fuck is that?
-Tapenade. Want some?

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:00.640
Who even are you?

00:17:00.720 --> 00:17:03.200
It's just something I wanna eat, Ryan.

00:17:03.280 --> 00:17:04.560
[phone beeps]

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:07.000
[gasps]

00:17:07.560 --> 00:17:09.080
Oh, my God.

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:12.240
-What is it?
-Naomi!

00:17:12.960 --> 00:17:14.040
Shit!

00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:19.320
Old school,<i> el perfecto</i> Naomi?
You guys keep in contact?

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:22.440
Ryan, just go! Go!

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:32.240
[Lacie] Oh, my God!
Nay-Nay, how are you? [giggles]

00:17:32.320 --> 00:17:34.640
I was just fixing myself a snack.

00:17:34.720 --> 00:17:39.560
<i>Oh, Lace, could I just say</i>
<i>I am so happy to see your face?</i>

00:17:39.640 --> 00:17:42.400
-Me too. It's been...
<i>-Too long.</i>

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:44.080
-Way too long.
<i>-And that's my fault.</i>

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.280
-No, it's mine. Everything is just so...
<i>-Everything's just so...</i>

00:17:47.360 --> 00:17:50.640
Crazy! Oh, it's so good to see you.

00:17:50.720 --> 00:17:54.200
<i>When you posted that Mr. Rags photo...</i>

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:56.200
I know, Mr. Rags!

00:17:56.280 --> 00:17:58.200
<i>I just had to call</i>

00:17:58.280 --> 00:18:01.520
<i>and talk to you because...</i>

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.520
<i>Whoo-hoo!</i>

00:18:03.600 --> 00:18:05.560
[screams, laughs]

00:18:05.640 --> 00:18:07.840
Wow! That's a... big ring! [laughs]

00:18:08.080 --> 00:18:12.760
Congratulations! Who's the, um... Paul?

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:16.360
<i>He is great. So smart. Just sweet.</i>

00:18:16.440 --> 00:18:18.200
<i>I know you're gonna love him.</i>

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.360
Uh-huh.

00:18:19.440 --> 00:18:21.120
<i>So, anyways, the big day...</i>

00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:22.360
Yes, when is it?

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:23.880
<i>So, we're getting married in a month</i>

00:18:23.960 --> 00:18:25.040
<i>on his family's estate</i>

00:18:25.120 --> 00:18:26.320
<i>up here on the island.</i>

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:29.120
<i>This place outside Port Mary, Honeysuckle.</i>
<i>You heard of it?</i>

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.200
No, but...

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:32.120
<i>Well, it's a private island.</i>

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:36.440
[singsong] <i>Take a looooook!</i>

00:18:36.520 --> 00:18:38.720
Oh, wow! That is... [giggles]

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:43.200
<i>I know, right? So... can you make it?</i>

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:45.720
Are you kidding? Of course.

00:18:46.360 --> 00:18:48.680
<i>Great, cool, cos I was wondering if...</i>

00:18:50.320 --> 00:18:52.200
<i>Lace, do you think...</i>

00:18:53.320 --> 00:18:54.720
<i>Would you be my maid of honour?</i>

00:18:55.600 --> 00:18:56.440
Seriously?

00:18:58.520 --> 00:18:59.600
Oh, my God.

00:19:02.280 --> 00:19:06.240
I mean, you've got such cool friends now.
Are you sure?

00:19:06.320 --> 00:19:11.000
<i>Remember when we used to plan our</i>
<i>dream weddings when we were, like, 11?</i>

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:14.760
-I know but we haven't s--
<i>-I don't know, just seeing Mr. Rags...</i>

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:19.360
<i>All the memories.</i>
<i>It just brought things home.</i>

00:19:19.440 --> 00:19:20.520
Oh, Nay-Nay.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:23.200
<i>I know we haven't kept in touch</i>
<i>as much as I'd have liked</i>

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:26.040
<i>and that is totally my fault,</i>
<i>but this is a big day.</i>

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:31.760
<i>A big life day and I want my oldest</i>
<i>friend with me, my oldest friend.</i>

00:19:31.840 --> 00:19:33.600
<i>I want you by my side.</i>

00:19:34.680 --> 00:19:38.200
Oh, my God. Thank you.

00:19:39.760 --> 00:19:41.120
What do I have to...

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:43.480
<i>Not much to it. A speech, mainly.</i>

00:19:43.560 --> 00:19:45.600
Speech? Of course!

00:19:45.680 --> 00:19:48.360
Mm-hmm. How big's the crowd?

00:19:48.440 --> 00:19:50.880
<i>Oh, my gosh, like...</i> [sings]<i> hundreds!</i>

00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:54.480
<i>It's a crazy guest list. I'll send it now.</i>

00:19:54.560 --> 00:19:57.480
<i>Paul's invited so many,</i>
<i>I don't want to call them big deals,</i>

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.600
<i>but they're all, like,</i>
<i>4.7 or above.</i>

00:20:01.680 --> 00:20:02.960
Uh-huh.

00:20:04.320 --> 00:20:08.240
Nay-Nay, I will not let you down.
[giggles]

00:20:08.320 --> 00:20:12.400
<i>Don't sweat too much!</i>
<i>Just talk about old memories.</i>

00:20:12.480 --> 00:20:15.000
-Sure.
