Blue thermos is coffee, red's whiskey.
Help yourself.

00:38:06.400 --> 00:38:08.240
I'm okay. Thanks.

00:38:09.280 --> 00:38:10.680
Where are you headed?

00:38:10.760 --> 00:38:15.560
Uh... Just as close as you can get
to Port Mary would be great. [laughs]

00:38:24.280 --> 00:38:27.080
Checking my feed for danger signs?

00:38:29.240 --> 00:38:34.160
I get it a lot.
1.4 gotta be an antisocial maniac, right?

00:38:34.960 --> 00:38:37.440
-You seem...
-Normal?

00:38:37.520 --> 00:38:39.720
-Yeah.
-Thank you.

00:38:41.320 --> 00:38:45.800
It took some effort.
What happened to you?

00:38:46.320 --> 00:38:50.560
I mean, you're a 2.8,
but you don't look 2.8.

00:38:50.640 --> 00:38:52.240
That's not-- This is temporary.

00:38:52.320 --> 00:38:54.440
-I'm gonna turn it around.
-Uh-huh.

00:38:54.520 --> 00:38:57.680
-I'm going to a wedding. Maid of honour.
-Nice.

00:38:57.760 --> 00:38:59.320
Wanna hear my speech?

00:39:00.160 --> 00:39:01.120
No.

00:39:04.840 --> 00:39:07.120
So how come you're a 2.8?

00:39:07.200 --> 00:39:10.640
Well, I got marked down
at the airport for yelling,

00:39:10.720 --> 00:39:13.320
and they put me on double damage.

00:39:13.400 --> 00:39:16.560
-How did it feel?
-Awful.

00:39:17.440 --> 00:39:18.880
I meant the yelling.

00:39:20.600 --> 00:39:22.800
I don't know. I was mad.

00:39:23.680 --> 00:39:25.880
Look at where it got me.

00:39:27.160 --> 00:39:31.040
But as long as I get to the wedding,
do the speech,

00:39:31.120 --> 00:39:33.520
they'll overlook the 2.8.
I'm with the bride.

00:39:33.600 --> 00:39:35.600
And if I do well,
well, they're all high fours

00:39:35.680 --> 00:39:36.880
so that velocitates my arc.

00:39:36.960 --> 00:39:40.560
And once they lift the point penalty,
well, my average goes way up,

00:39:40.640 --> 00:39:43.200
and, yeah, it's gonna be okay.

00:39:46.440 --> 00:39:48.480
God, you remind me of me.

00:39:48.560 --> 00:39:51.000
-Hmm.
-Not now.

00:39:52.880 --> 00:39:56.560
I was, uh... 4.6 once.

00:39:58.640 --> 00:40:01.360
-4.6?
-Used to live for it.

00:40:02.640 --> 00:40:04.960
All the work I put in...

00:40:07.840 --> 00:40:11.120
Eight years ago,
Tom, my husband, got cancer.

00:40:11.200 --> 00:40:16.440
It was pancreatic. It was a real bitch.
The symptoms showed up late.

00:40:17.480 --> 00:40:19.000
I'm so sorry.

00:40:20.200 --> 00:40:22.440
You don't know me
so you're not really sorry.

00:40:22.520 --> 00:40:26.760
You're just mainly awkward 
cos I have sprung some cancer talk at you.

00:40:27.880 --> 00:40:30.320
Anyway, I five-starred every doctor,

00:40:30.400 --> 00:40:34.960
every nurse, every high-four
consultant that we had.

00:40:35.040 --> 00:40:36.800
Ding. Ding. Ding. Thank you so much.

00:40:36.880 --> 00:40:39.600
The cancer didn't give a shit.
It just kept growing.

00:40:40.680 --> 00:40:44.720
A couple of months in, we heard
about this experimental treatment.

00:40:44.800 --> 00:40:48.480
It was very expensive. It was very exclusive.

00:40:49.520 --> 00:40:53.480
I did everything I could
to get him a spot there.

00:40:54.800 --> 00:40:57.960
Tom was a 4.3.

00:40:59.920 --> 00:41:02.440
They gave his bed to a 4.4.

00:41:07.440 --> 00:41:11.600
So when he died I thought, fuck it.

00:41:13.320 --> 00:41:16.000
I started saying what I wanted,
when I wanted.

00:41:16.080 --> 00:41:17.560
Just drop it out there.

00:41:18.640 --> 00:41:20.120
People don't always like that.

00:41:21.080 --> 00:41:24.400
It is incredible
how fast you slip off the ladder

00:41:24.480 --> 00:41:26.160
when you start doing that.

00:41:26.240 --> 00:41:30.760
It turned out a lot of my friends
didn't care for honesty.

00:41:32.840 --> 00:41:37.080
Treated me like I had taken a shit
at their breakfast table.

00:41:37.160 --> 00:41:41.160
But, Jesus Christ, it felt good.

00:41:41.240 --> 00:41:43.720
Shedding those fuckers.

00:41:44.800 --> 00:41:47.480
It was like taking off tight shoes.

00:41:47.960 --> 00:41:51.160
-Maybe you should try it?
-Oh, come on. [laughs]

00:41:51.240 --> 00:41:52.520
Why not?

00:41:52.600 --> 00:41:57.240
I can't just kick off my shoes
and walk the earth or whatever.

00:41:57.320 --> 00:42:00.680
-You won't know unless you try.
-Oh, that's just...

00:42:03.040 --> 00:42:06.000
Look, you had something with your life,

00:42:06.080 --> 00:42:11.760
real things, good things,
and you lost it all, and I'm sorry.

00:42:11.840 --> 00:42:16.400
So now you've got nothing left to lose.

00:42:16.480 --> 00:42:19.320
But I don't even have the something
worth losing, not yet.

00:42:19.400 --> 00:42:22.840
You know,
I mean, I'm still fighting for that.

00:42:24.680 --> 00:42:30.040
-And what is "that"?
-I don't know. Enough. To be content?

00:42:31.120 --> 00:42:36.400
Like, to look around and think,
well, I guess I'm okay.

00:42:37.160 --> 00:42:42.000
Just to be able to breathe out,
not feeling like... like...

00:42:43.320 --> 00:42:49.360
Like just...
And that is way off, like, way, way off.

00:42:49.440 --> 00:42:52.280
And until I get there,
I have to play the numbers game.

00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:57.080
We all do, that's what we're in.
That's how the fucking world works.

00:42:58.640 --> 00:43:03.120
Look, maybe you don't remember,
you know, you're just too old to get it.

00:43:05.200 --> 00:43:07.200
I do not mean that how it sounds.

00:43:09.520 --> 00:43:12.240
Don't worry. I'm not voting you down.

00:43:36.960 --> 00:43:40.360
-Sweetheart.
-[gasps] What time is it?

00:43:40.440 --> 00:43:44.680
I'm heading east from here so I think
you need to get yourself another ride.

00:43:44.760 --> 00:43:47.840
-Where are we?
-About 30 miles from Port Mary.

00:43:47.920 --> 00:43:51.160
A lot of buses stop here
so you should be fine.

00:43:51.240 --> 00:43:54.480
-Well, thank you.
-Good luck with your speech.

00:43:54.560 --> 00:43:56.160
[laughs]

00:43:57.080 --> 00:43:59.880
I put a little something in there
for you.

00:43:59.960 --> 00:44:03.000
-You did?
-Emergency escape hatch!

00:44:06.800 --> 00:44:07.720
Bye.

00:44:22.480 --> 00:44:25.760
[Lacie] In this world,
we're all so caught up...

00:44:25.840 --> 00:44:28.000
-[door opens]
-...in our own dramas.

00:44:28.080 --> 00:44:31.240
-[girl] So, Dad was like...
-It's easy to forget what matters.

00:44:31.320 --> 00:44:32.520
[girl] He'd never even heard of the show.

00:44:32.600 --> 00:44:34.880
I'm like, "You never heard
of<i> Sea of Tranquillity?"</i>

00:44:34.960 --> 00:44:37.600
Like, the number-one sci-fi fantasy,

00:44:37.680 --> 00:44:39.600
and he's all like, "What the fuck?" Whatever!

00:44:39.680 --> 00:44:41.840
I think I'm allergic to this purple.

00:44:41.920 --> 00:44:45.160
So I'm like, "Well, I'm going
to Tranquillity Con in Port Mary.

00:44:45.240 --> 00:44:47.840
That's why I'm dressed
like Lieutenant Duster."

00:44:47.920 --> 00:44:50.760
He's all like, "Uh... Port Mary is
frickin' miles away."

00:44:50.840 --> 00:44:51.880
Yadda, yadda, yadda.

00:44:51.960 --> 00:44:56.760
-[toilet flushes]
-He one-stars me. Like, thanks, Dad.

00:44:56.840 --> 00:45:00.240
-[girl 1] See you back on there.
-[girl 2] Okay.

00:45:03.920 --> 00:45:07.840
Are you guys headed to Tranquillity Con?

00:45:07.920 --> 00:45:10.880
-You're into<i> Sea of Tranquillity?</i>
-Totally.

00:45:10.960 --> 00:45:12.480
I was all set to go.

00:45:12.560 --> 00:45:18.280
My friend, who is there already,
has my costume, but my car broke down.

00:45:18.960 --> 00:45:21.640
Well, there's some space in the RV.

00:45:30.600 --> 00:45:32.600
-Hi.
-Hey!

00:45:32.680 --> 00:45:34.760
-You're a Trank head, huh?
-Sorry?

00:45:34.840 --> 00:45:37.080
Trank head.<i> Sea of Tranquillity</i> fan?

00:45:37.160 --> 00:45:40.720
Oh, yeah.
We say Tranksters where I'm from.

00:45:40.800 --> 00:45:44.360
-Who's your favourite character?
-Gotta be Lieutenant Duster.

00:45:44.440 --> 00:45:46.200
-She's awesome.
-She?

00:45:46.280 --> 00:45:48.480
He! I misspoke.

00:45:48.560 --> 00:45:51.240
Lieutenant Duster has no fixed gender.

00:45:51.320 --> 00:45:54.840
I know, and that's why
it's so hard to remember, right?

00:45:54.920 --> 00:45:56.880
-[ringtone playing]
-Excuse me. Gotta get this.

00:45:56.960 --> 00:45:59.640
My friend, at the convention. [giggles]

00:46:01.880 --> 00:46:03.720
Hi, Nay! [laughs]

00:46:03.800 --> 00:46:09.080
So, oh, my God,
insane night, but I am so close now.

00:46:09.160 --> 00:46:10.680
[Naomi]<i> Don't come.</i>

00:46:10.760 --> 00:46:14.280
What? No. No. I'm, like, an hour away.

00:46:14.360 --> 00:46:16.320
Don't come. I don't want you here.

00:46:16.400 --> 00:46:19.920
I don't know what is up with you,
but I cannot have a 2.6 at my wedding.

00:46:20.000 --> 00:46:23.280
Oh, no, that's temporary!
That's temporary.

00:46:23.360 --> 00:46:25.600
<i>Well, the wedding's today so...</i>

00:46:25.680 --> 00:46:28.160
-But it doesn't change anything.
<i>-Lacie...</i>

00:46:28.240 --> 00:46:30.360
-I can still do the same speech.
<i>-Lacie...</i>

00:46:30.440 --> 00:46:33.680
-And there's Mr. Rags!
-No!

00:46:33.760 --> 00:46:36.360
<i>But... But you invited me.</i>

00:46:36.440 --> 00:46:39.040
You've seen the guest list.
They are all, like, 4.5 or above.

00:46:39.120 --> 00:46:42.480
They are going to freak at a 2.6,
and I am not taking that kind of damage,

00:46:42.560 --> 00:46:45.200
plus I haven't dipped under
a 4.7 in, like, six months.

00:46:46.760 --> 00:46:50.200
You said you wanted your oldest friend.

00:46:50.280 --> 00:46:53.360
<i>When I asked you to speak,</i>
<i>you were a 4.2, okay?</i>

00:46:53.440 --> 00:46:56.760
And the authenticity of a vintage bond
low four at a gathering of this calibre

00:46:56.840 --> 00:46:59.800
played fantastically
on all the simulations we ran.

00:46:59.880 --> 00:47:02.080
Forecast was a prestige bounce
of .2 minimum.

00:47:02.160 --> 00:47:05.680
But now you're a sub three. Sorry.

00:47:05.760 --> 00:47:07.400
That just puts the stink on things
a little too much.

00:47:07.480 --> 00:47:09.600
That just plays badly for us.

00:47:09.680 --> 00:47:12.080
So it was just about numbers for you?

00:47:12.160 --> 00:47:15.240
Oh, cut the shit!
It was numbers for both of us.

00:47:15.320 --> 00:47:17.200
<i>You wanted those primo votes,</i>
<i>don't deny it.</i>

00:47:17.280 --> 00:47:20.280
<i>It's not like you could get them</i>
<i>on your own. Let's not kid ourselves.</i>

00:47:20.360 --> 00:47:22.720
Oh, I'm... I'm getting those votes.

00:47:22.800 --> 00:47:26.080
What? You're just gonna roll up here
and make people like you?

00:47:26.160 --> 00:47:30.760
-That's right. I'm doing my speech.
-No, you're not.

00:47:30.840 --> 00:47:35.200
Yes, I am. And they are gonna vote me
through the roof when they hear it.

00:47:35.280 --> 00:47:40.280
-Weep their fucking eyes out!
-Go home!

00:47:40.360 --> 00:47:43.320
-[phone beeping]
-Hello?

00:47:43.400 --> 00:47:45.960
[sighs] Fuck!

00:47:48.680 --> 00:47:51.800
I have never seen
your stupid fucking show.

00:47:52.400 --> 00:47:53.560
[tyres screech]

00:47:57.560 --> 00:48:00.200
[shouts] Hope they cancel it!

00:48:11.400 --> 00:48:13.800
-[horn honks]
-I need a ride!

00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:16.320
[shouts]

00:48:16.400 --> 00:48:19.040
-[phone beeping]
-Fuck!

00:48:22.680 --> 00:48:24.160
Jesus!

00:48:27.760 --> 00:48:29.440
[engine roars]

00:48:40.080 --> 00:48:42.240
Hey! Hey!

00:48:42.840 --> 00:48:43.880
Hey!

00:48:45.840 --> 00:48:48.240
-Can I borrow your bike?
-What?

00:48:48.320 --> 00:48:51.440
Can I borrow your bike?

00:48:51.520 --> 00:48:56.440
Do you, Naomi Jayne Blestow,
take this man to be your husband,

00:48:56.520 --> 00:48:59.440
to live together with him
in the covenant of marriage?

00:49:00.360 --> 00:49:02.400
To love him, comfort him,

00:49:02.480 --> 00:49:06.080
honour and keep him,
in sickness and in health...

00:49:06.160 --> 00:49:09.560
and forsaking all others,
be faithful unto him...

00:49:19.040 --> 00:49:21.520
[cheering and applause]

00:49:36.600 --> 00:49:38.720
[indistinct radio chatter]

00:49:43.480 --> 00:49:44.720
[revs engine]

00:49:51.720 --> 00:49:53.120
[screams]

00:50:12.080 --> 00:50:14.280
[applause]

00:50:14.360 --> 00:50:17.400
To my best mate, Anthony.
Let's hear it for him.

00:50:17.480 --> 00:50:19.000
[cheering]

00:50:19.080 --> 00:50:22.480
You've been there from day one.
I love you, man. I appreciate you.

00:50:22.560 --> 00:50:26.040
Hilarious speech, by the way.
By your standards.

00:50:26.120 --> 00:50:27.360
[laughter]

00:50:27.440 --> 00:50:30.280
-Pow! Pow! Pow!
-Oh! Oh! Oh! [laughs]

00:50:30.360 --> 00:50:33.960
[Paul] He's still got a few bullets left.
Oh, man.

00:50:34.040 --> 00:50:36.080
Oh, gosh, well, um...

00:50:38.800 --> 00:50:40.240
[gasps] Shit!

00:50:40.800 --> 00:50:44.720
[Paul] We have so many people to thank.
Our beautiful bridesmaids.

00:50:44.800 --> 00:50:46.600
-[cheering]
-But, of course,

00:50:46.680 --> 00:50:51.680
my most heartfelt thanks,
my warmest thanks,

00:50:51.760 --> 00:50:55.040
are to someone who's my best friend,

00:50:56.320 --> 00:51:03.160
my lover and now,
I'm honoured to say, my wife.

00:51:03.240 --> 00:51:05.760
-Naomi!
-[cheering and whooping]

00:51:08.000 --> 00:51:13.080
-[cheering]
-[Paul] One, two, three! Naomi!

00:51:14.560 --> 00:51:17.360
-[man] The A Team!
-[phone beeps]

00:51:17.440 --> 00:51:18.800
I love you so much, darl.

00:51:18.880 --> 00:51:20.400
Whoo-whoo-whoo-whoo!

00:51:20.480 --> 00:51:22.440
[man] Congratulations, sir.

00:51:22.520 --> 00:51:24.320
-Thank you. 
-No, thank you.

00:51:24.400 --> 00:51:26.480
-[whooping]
-Get over here!

00:51:26.560 --> 00:51:28.080
Get your ass over here.

00:51:28.160 --> 00:51:30.760
-Get in here, big boy.
-[phones beep]

00:51:30.840 --> 00:51:32.880
-You're beautiful!
-[cheering]

00:51:34.840 --> 00:51:37.760
Yeah! Gimme five! Good choice!

00:51:37.840 --> 00:51:40.240
You fucking earned it, man.
You fucking earned it.

00:51:41.760 --> 00:51:43.000
[giggles nervously]

00:51:44.640 --> 00:51:46.400
Everybody, hello!

00:51:46.480 --> 00:51:48.520
-Oh, my God.
-I love you.

00:51:52.520 --> 00:51:56.320
Can everyone be quiet for a moment?

00:51:58.440 --> 00:52:00.040
Thank you. [giggles]

00:52:01.400 --> 00:52:03.520
-Get rid of her.
-That would play awful.

00:52:03.600 --> 00:52:04.840
She's a fucking 1.1.

00:52:04.920 --> 00:52:10.280
Now for those of you who don't know me,
which is... all of you...

00:52:10.360 --> 00:52:14.320
my name is Lacie Pound

00:52:14.400 --> 00:52:18.240
and, believe it or not,
I am one of Naomi's oldest friends.

00:52:18.840 --> 00:52:20.960
Hi, Nay-Nay!

00:52:22.240 --> 00:52:25.280
It's great to meet you too, Paul.
I've heard a lot about you.

00:52:25.360 --> 00:52:27.160
He's a pretty big deal, that Paul.

00:52:27.240 --> 00:52:29.640
-Pretty big deal.
-[camera shutter clicks]

00:52:29.720 --> 00:52:33.360
He makes his own tapenade! Yeah.

00:52:33.440 --> 00:52:35.440
[laughs] Uh...

00:52:37.720 --> 00:52:39.920
Anyway, um... I...

00:52:41.600 --> 00:52:46.000
have looked up to Naomi
pretty much my entire life.

00:52:46.080 --> 00:52:47.960
We met when we were five years old,

00:52:48.040 --> 00:52:52.200
and right up through to our
teenage years, we made quite the pair.

00:52:52.920 --> 00:52:55.160
We'd talk about all the things
girls talk about,

00:52:55.240 --> 00:53:01.520
you know, boys, hair, products,
uh... more boys. [laughs]

00:53:01.600 --> 00:53:05.160
I mean, I tried sometimes
to expand our range a little

00:53:05.240 --> 00:53:09.920
and talk about climate change,
but she found that kind of boring so...

00:53:10.560 --> 00:53:11.920
Go on.

00:53:12.000 --> 00:53:14.840
She was probably right.
I mean, fuck the planet, right?

00:53:14.920 --> 00:53:16.440
Whoo!

00:53:16.520 --> 00:53:20.960
Yes, thank you! Come on.
Let's have a little fun here.

00:53:21.040 --> 00:53:23.560
You know, fuck the planet! [laughs]

00:53:23.640 --> 00:53:26.040
-[shouts] Fuck the planet!
-[feedback]

00:53:26.120 --> 00:53:27.600
[crockery rattles]

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:30.880
-[phone beeps]
-Anyway...

00:53:31.960 --> 00:53:38.920
I... looked up to Naomi
pretty much my entire life,

00:53:39.000 --> 00:53:44.280
which meant she was looking down on me.

00:53:45.160 --> 00:53:48.120
Always with a smile though. [laughs]

00:53:48.200 --> 00:53:52.760
In high school,
she was my shoulder to cry on.

00:53:52.840 --> 00:53:58.120
She seemed to enjoy that.
Guys and me never worked out.

00:53:58.200 --> 00:54:02.760
They'd see Naomi and just...
Whoo! You know, that was it.

00:54:03.640 --> 00:54:09.480
She had this tight ass,

00:54:09.560 --> 00:54:12.680
like two fists.

00:54:12.760 --> 00:54:14.440
Uh-huh.

00:54:14.520 --> 00:54:17.560
[giggles] I was all like...

00:54:17.640 --> 00:54:19.760
[giggles]

00:54:21.200 --> 00:54:23.680
I was like...

00:54:23.760 --> 00:54:25.600
through the hallways in high school.

00:54:27.000 --> 00:54:29.160
[cackling]

00:54:30.840 --> 00:54:32.440
[phones beep]

00:54:37.000 --> 00:54:38.840
[cries]

00:54:44.000 --> 00:54:45.720
And she was there for me.

00:54:48.160 --> 00:54:49.600
Holding my hair back...

00:54:51.240 --> 00:54:56.480
as I knelt,
vomiting, in front of the crapper.

00:55:01.080 --> 00:55:04.560
Thank you for that, Naomi.

00:55:07.600 --> 00:55:09.480
I always wished I was you.

00:55:11.760 --> 00:55:13.040
And...

00:55:14.000 --> 00:55:16.360
I guess that's why you kept me around
so long?

00:55:19.560 --> 00:55:22.520
Until you got your new job

00:55:22.600 --> 00:55:27.560
and your fancy new friends.

00:55:29.520 --> 00:55:31.880
And that...

00:55:31.960 --> 00:55:33.760
[laughs]

00:55:33.840 --> 00:55:36.960
...fucking... jackhole!

00:55:37.880 --> 00:55:41.240
And you didn't need me.
You probably got another me.

00:55:41.320 --> 00:55:46.680
Guess there's some other "yeth Beth"
you moved on to like a succubus.

00:55:46.760 --> 00:55:49.520
-[phones beeping]
-I'm getting to Mr. Rags, okay? Jesus!

00:55:50.360 --> 00:55:53.280
-[crowd gasps]
-Stay back.

00:55:54.760 --> 00:55:57.760
Stay the fuck back! I'll kill him!

00:55:57.840 --> 00:55:59.680
I'll cut his head off
and stick it up my ass!

00:55:59.760 --> 00:56:01.000
[gasps]

00:56:02.080 --> 00:56:04.520
[gasps] Time's nearly up!

00:56:04.600 --> 00:56:05.720
-Hey! Calm down.
-I...

00:56:05.800 --> 00:56:10.800
I just wanted to say, in this world
so caught up in our own shit,

00:56:10.880 --> 00:56:14.280
-let's not forget what matters.
-It's okay. It's okay.

00:56:14.960 --> 00:56:20.840
Happiness, fucking Paul and Naomi,
and she's...

00:56:21.320 --> 00:56:25.440
She... She fucked Greg!

00:56:27.200 --> 00:56:28.960
I know she did.

00:56:30.040 --> 00:56:32.920
-I know you did.
-No...

00:56:33.000 --> 00:56:35.280
Don't even try to deny--

00:56:35.360 --> 00:56:37.680
-[screams]
-[feedback screeches]

00:56:37.760 --> 00:56:43.120
The little girl who, when we were
just five-years-old in art camp,

00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:46.880
started talking to me
because she saw I was scared

00:56:47.560 --> 00:56:50.000
and helped me make Mr. Rags.

00:56:50.080 --> 00:56:55.600
He reminds me of you
and what you meant to me then!

00:56:55.680 --> 00:56:59.240
[cries] And I'm so honoured to be here
to see this shit!

00:57:00.160 --> 00:57:05.360
[screams] I love you, Nay-Nay!
I've always loved you!

00:57:06.400 --> 00:57:08.720
I love you!

00:57:09.960 --> 00:57:11.040
[camera shutter clicking]

00:57:26.200 --> 00:57:28.520
[whirring]

00:58:39.560 --> 00:58:42.360
[breathes deeply]

00:59:20.120 --> 00:59:21.840
[sobs]

00:59:21.920 --> 00:59:23.320
[laughs]

00:59:53.920 --> 00:59:55.720
What the fuck are you looking at?

00:59:55.800 --> 00:59:57.840
Just what I was wondering.

00:59:58.400 --> 00:59:59.120
Well...

01:00:01.080 --> 01:00:02.000
Don't!

01:00:02.760 --> 01:00:05.720
Don't? Don't wonder?

01:00:05.800 --> 01:00:06.960
Uh-huh.

01:00:07.560 --> 01:00:12.680
-It would be a dull world without wonder.
-I don't give a shit about your world.

01:00:13.520 --> 01:00:15.440
I don't like your brassiere.

01:00:18.840 --> 01:00:20.320
I don't like your moustache.

01:00:21.720 --> 01:00:23.520
I don't like your aura.

01:00:23.600 --> 01:00:25.840
-My aura?
-Yeah.

01:00:27.560 --> 01:00:31.360
I don't like your... head.

01:00:31.440 --> 01:00:34.120
Your entire head is just ridiculous to me.

01:00:34.200 --> 01:00:35.360
Really?

01:00:35.440 --> 01:00:41.240
You look like an alcoholic
former weatherman.

01:00:41.320 --> 01:00:43.800
You sound like a lost little lamb

01:00:43.880 --> 01:00:46.360
that just got told there's no Santa Claus.

01:00:47.600 --> 01:00:50.320
What sort of cartoon character
did your mum have to fuck

01:00:50.400 --> 01:00:52.000
to brew you up in the womb?

01:00:52.080 --> 01:00:53.760
At least I look like I was born,

01:00:53.840 --> 01:00:58.320
not shit out by some tormented
cow creature in an underground lab.

01:00:58.400 --> 01:01:00.080
You got tossed out of that lab.

01:01:00.160 --> 01:01:02.640
-Oh, yeah?
-Oh, yeah, flushed out.

01:01:02.720 --> 01:01:05.560
-Ooh!
-In the trash!

01:01:05.640 --> 01:01:09.200
-Your face is a fucking...
-Fucking.

01:01:09.280 --> 01:01:13.160
Fucking biological car crash

01:01:13.240 --> 01:01:15.240
that made Picasso screw his eyes up
and say,

01:01:15.320 --> 01:01:16.800
"Well, that just don't make sense."

01:01:16.880 --> 01:01:18.600
[laughs]

01:01:18.680 --> 01:01:21.280
-You're a fucking asshole.
-Fuck you!

01:01:21.360 --> 01:01:24.040
-Fuck you next Wednesday.
-Fuck you for Christmas!

01:01:24.120 --> 01:01:28.960
-Fuck you!
-Fuck you!